Byte-by-byte Description of file: pca.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bytes   Format Units  Label  Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1- 5   F5.3   ---    Phase   Pulsation phase (phase 0 at minimum radius) (1)
 7-16   F10.6  km.s-1 Vmean   Mean RV curve of the training set (2)
18-29   F12.9  ---    PC1     Principal component 1 (3)
31-42   F12.9  ---    PC2     Principal component 2 (3)
44-55   F12.9  ---    PC3     Principal component 3 (3)
57-68   F12.9  ---    PC4     Principal component 4 (3)
70-81   F12.9  ---    PC5     Principal component 5 (3)
83-94   F12.9  ---    PC6     Principal component 6 (3)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (1): 1000 equally spaced points, 0 <= phase < 1 (step 0.001).
    The curves are periodic: phase 1 is equivalent to phase 0.
Note (2): Mean of the training-set curves, with vgamma removed.
Note (3): Unit-norm eigenvectors (sum of squares over the grid = 1),
    ordered by explained variance ratio, in %:
    66.23, 16.22, 11.86, 2.75, 1.69, 0.43
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Byte-by-byte Description of file: coeffs.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Bytes   Format Units  Label  Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 19   A19    ---    Name    Cepheid name, as in VELOCE-I
 21- 25   A5     ---    Set     [test/train] PCA training or test set (4)
 27- 34   F8.6   [d]    logP    Log of the pulsation period (VELOCE-I)
 36- 44   F9.4   km.s-1 p1      Coefficient of PC1 (5)
 46- 54   F9.4   km.s-1 p2      Coefficient of PC2 (5)
 56- 64   F9.4   km.s-1 p3      Coefficient of PC3 (5)
 66- 74   F9.4   km.s-1 p4      Coefficient of PC4 (5)
 76- 84   F9.4   km.s-1 p5      Coefficient of PC5 (5)
 86- 94   F9.4   km.s-1 p6      Coefficient of PC6 (5)
 96-104   F9.6   ---    dphi   ? Phase offset between Gaia DR3 G-band epoch and
                               minimum radius (6)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (4): The PCs and the KDE priors were derived from the training set
    only; the test set was used for validation.
Note (5): Coefficients p_i of the PC model fitted to the star's VELOCE-I
    Fourier-series model (Eq. 1 of the paper).
Note (6): dphi = [((E_GaiaDR3 - E_VELOCE)/P_VELOCE + 0.5) mod 1] - 0.5
    (Eq. 2 of the paper). Missing when the star is absent from the Gaia
    DR3 vari_cepheid table or the phase drift exceeds 0.1.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Byte-by-byte Description of file: kde.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bytes   Format Units  Label  Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1- 4   A4     ---    Prior   [PC/dphi] Prior to which the row applies (7)
 6- 9   A4     ---    Var     Variable of the KDE (column label in coeffs.dat)
11-14   A4     ---    Unit    Unit of bw, Min and Max (9)
16-30   E15.8  ---    bw      Gaussian kernel bandwidth (cv_ml)
32-46   E15.8  ---    Min     Lower bound of the prior domain (8)
48-62   E15.8  ---    Max     Upper bound of the prior domain (8)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (7): PC = 7-D KDE of (logP, p1,...,p6); dphi = 2-D KDE of
    (logP, dphi). Both use Gaussian product kernels (statsmodels
    KDEMultivariate, var_type='c'*n, bw='cv_ml') on the training set.
    The prior at a given period is the KDE conditioned on logP.
Note (8): Training-set minimum and maximum, extended by 10% of the
    training-set range on each side.
Note (9): [d] = decimal logarithm of a period in days (CDS convention).
    For logP, bw is a width in log P, i.e. in dex.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Byte-by-byte Description of file: tableb1.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bytes   Format Units  Label    Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1-12   A12    ---    Name      Cepheid identifier (10)
14-16   A3     ---    Gal       [LMC/SMC] Host galaxy
18-28   A11    ---    Ref       Source of the RV time series (10)
30-35   F6.2   km.s-1 vgamma    Pulsation-averaged (systemic) velocity (11)
37-40   F4.2   km.s-1 e_vgamma  Uncertainty on vgamma
42-46   F5.2   km.s-1 P2Pvgcl  ? Peak-to-peak variation of the cluster-averaged
                               vgamma (11)
48-52   F5.2   km.s-1 P2P       Peak-to-peak pulsation amplitude of the model
54-57   F4.2   km.s-1 RMSE      Root-mean-square error of the fit
59-61   F3.1   %      RMSE/P2P  Ratio of RMSE to P2P
63-63   A1     ---    SB1       [YN] Evidence of orbital motion (11)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (10): LMC: names and RV time series from Storm et al.
    (2011A&A...534A..95S); SMC: OGLE identifiers and RV time series from
    Gieren et al. (2018A&A...620A..99G).
Note (11): For SB1=Y stars, results of the hierarchical fit with
    cluster-specific vgamma (M_RV^MULTI) and P2P of the cluster-averaged
    vgamma; otherwise results of the single-vgamma fit (M_RV^SOLO).
    SMC-CEP-0524 formally exceeds the f_sigma,cluster threshold but is
    considered probably single (Sect. 4.4 of the paper).
